<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaborone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1964</span> · Also known as Gaberones</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaborone is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, in the south-east of the country near the South African border. It was built from 1964 as a planned capital for independence, since the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> had been run from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahikeng">Mafikeng</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. It takes its name from Kgosi Gaborone, a Batlokwa chief whose village stood nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaborone.jpg" alt="Gaborone" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNJerem · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_I-Tower_SE_20200712.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
